# Minikube manifests for AJS Suite
# ⚠️ WARNING: Minikube on a t3.micro will NOT run ELK + Grafana + app together.
# Resource math won't work — Elasticsearch alone needs ~2GB RAM, Grafana needs ~256MB,
# and the app needs ~128MB. A t3.micro has only 1GB RAM and 1 vCPU.
#
# Recommended: Deploy the app via Docker Compose on the EC2 directly (as this project
# is configured for). Use Minikube only for lightweight services or on a more powerful
# machine (t3.medium+, or a dedicated Kubernetes host).
#
# This directory contains minimal manifests for reference only.

# To start Minikube (on a more powerful machine):
#   minikube start --memory=4096 --cpus=2
#
# To deploy the app:
#   kubectl apply -f k8s/minikube/

# For the current Docker Compose-based deployment on EC2, see:
#   - compose.yaml (main app: admin + web/nginx)
#   - monitoring/docker-compose.yaml (Prometheus + Grafana — optional)
#   - elk/docker-compose.yaml (ELK stack — heavy, separate host recommended)

# Minikube resource estimate:
#   App (Docker Compose): ~256MB RAM
#   Prometheus + Grafana: ~512MB RAM
#   ELK Stack (Elasticsearch alone): ~2GB RAM minimum
#   t3.micro: 1GB RAM, 1 vCPU — INSUFFICIENT for ELK + Grafana + app
#   t3.medium: 4GB RAM, 2 vCPU — BARELY sufficient for app + Grafana, not ELK